  "reason": "Evidence: config_003 (pca_n2000, resnet50, avgpool, weighted) is the best at 0.639 acc, and config_034 shows scgpt is far inferior to pca_n2000 (~0.11 gap). config_008 shows weighted fusion slightly beats concat. However, we have zero information about the image encoder axis—only resnet50 has been tested. Question: Does upgrading the image encoder to imagenet_vit_l (a larger, more expressive ViT) improve performance when paired with the best-known RNA encoder (pca_n2000), aggregation (avgpool), and fusion (weighted)? config_051 is a clean single-variable change from config_003, isolating the image encoder effect. Rationale: With 6 experiments remaining, we need to resolve whether a stronger image backbone is worth pursuing, as this decision gates many downstream combinations (e.g., whether to pair vit_l with transformer aggregation or scvi_n200). Testing this major architectural axis early maximizes information gain per experiment."
